Patch 6007: PAD_SCRIPT events "+N:mask" (N clock units after the previous event fired) and "~N:mask" (once the
previous event has fired, at least 1 s has passed and no file has been read for N ms).

Fixed-time routes need long safety gaps for loading screens, so a scripted Free Battle took about 8 minutes to reach
the fight. With "+" and "~" a route follows the game however long each screen takes. Every event now also waits for
the one before it; absolute events keep their meaning. ppu_fs_idle_ms() reports the time since the last guest read.

